{"commit": "5241919f48c3bf54fbe8d4e9d50b4a55038da150", "id": "5241919f48c3bf54fbe8d4e9d50b4a55038da150-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Selected test is not present at the fixed revision: regression::blank_matches_nothing_between_space_and_tab", "repo": "https://github.com/rust-lang/regex", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T002416Z-b202ba87", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/5241919f48c3bf54fbe8d4e9d50b4a55038da150-1/20260924T002416Z-b202ba87/origin.json": "6fef0e323ebe4086186ea6085989c8d4e29bb34cba4405b6135099599e672d7c", "evidence/5241919f48c3bf54fbe8d4e9d50b4a55038da150-1/20260924T002416Z-b202ba87/proposal.json": "3be9096c4b612b4b281fa5c7223d9f1035c76261b00f12aa064a49a5e77442a3"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "regex-syntax", "status": "blocked", "subject": "syntax: fix [[:blank:]] character class", "summary": "When `regex-syntax` was rewritten, a transcription error in the ASCII `Blank` class table left the entry as `[(' ', '\\t')]` (a single inverted-range tuple) instead of `[('\\t', '\\t'), (' ', ' ')]`. Because the class normalizer expanded that into the byte interval `[0x09, 0x20]`, the POSIX `[[:blank:]]` class matched control characters and most punctuation in addition to the intended `[ \\t]`.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:24:16.702038+00:00"}
